WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.160
I had no idea what this crime was
or how it could possibly work

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.440
Until I started looking into it.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.120
The first we knew about sextortion
was a case in Scotland,

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.480
involving a 17-year-old lad
called Daniel Perry,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.600
who had apparently received
messages through Facebook.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.520
He had some money extorted from him.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.480
They received sums of
about 3,000 pounds (US$3,750)

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.120
from him before he ran out of money.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.680
They then carried on threatening him,

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:51.400
threatening to release
these video recordings of him.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.920
And they started saying to him
Why don't you kill yourself?

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.280
They were taunting him even.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.280
In the last message
he sent to them, he said,

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.160
I haven't got any more money, bye bye.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.520
He then took his own life.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.280
When the PNP Anti Cybercrime
Group was created

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:47.000
There were a lot of reports of sextortion
happening in the Philippines,

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.720
victimising foreign nationals.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.800
Of course, international pressure
started to build,

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.760
especially after the death
of Daniel Perry in 2013,

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.280
and the Interpol was involved.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.160
There was one,

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.040
I suppose a typical victim,
of a guy in Hong Kong.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.960
He was working in an office
and was approached on Facebook.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.880
And he went off into the office toilets.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:40.960
He had this exchange with somebody
he thought was a woman in the Philippines.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.160
Two hours later, they were
demanding money from him.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.880
He had to rush out of the office
at the end of the day,

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:05.160
to try and find a Western Union branch
to send over a sum of money.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.040
The next day, another demand came.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:12.600
He eventually sent about 2,000
to 3,000 pounds, or about US$3,000,

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:16.520
before plucking up the courage
to go to the police and report it.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:27.120
Usually, these crimes might originate
in Nigeria or some African countries,

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.720
and then get copied overseas,

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.960
but this was the first that anyone had ever
heard of these crimes being perpetrated.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.720
In around 2013 or 2014,
they suddenly started springing up.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.400
This crime didn't exist
until Maria Caparas invented it.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:45.160
The ringleader of a group
of young people

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:48.520
who were carrying out
these crimes of sextortion,

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:52.320
extorting money from people
through Facebook

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.560
and getting large sums of money out of it.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.360
Her syndicate is thought to have
raked in millions of pounds.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.720
Huge sums of untraceable money,

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.960
all of which will be sent
to Western Union accounts.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:09.920
Some of the Western Union branches
in the area where she lived,

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:14.080
recorded the biggest takings of any
Western Union branches in the world

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.960
for a period in 2014 and 2015.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.880
There was so much money
coming in at that time.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.480
This operation was named
Operation Strikeback

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:39.800
which resulted in the crackdown
of the syndicate group

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:43.240
which was involved in sextortion cases.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.560
It was quite big, because

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:16.640
back then, cybersex extortion
or crime was new to us.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:27.120
It was not that popular yet,
so the impact of the story was alarming.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.640
They were able to track
the movements of money.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:41.640
All the proceeds were going
to the two Western Union accounts

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:46.600
owned by Caparas and her live-in partner.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:51.800
I think they were able to seize
a couple of laptops.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:11:00.000
Hard disks, sex toys, several
motor vehicles, including wigs

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.320
I was told that she was still active
on social media in prison.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:31.160
I sent her a message, in hope
rather than expectation, saying,

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:36.320
I'd like to hear your side of the story,
would you let me visit you in prison?

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.200
She insisted she was innocent,

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:54.400
that another woman in the village
was the real kingpin

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.360
and she was being scapegoated.

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:02.320
She almost convinced me.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:06.520
She told me that she had been
set up, and she was crying.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:09.960
And I asked her, What do you think
about the men who fall for this?

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:13.280
She said, They're stupid,
they're just stupid. I told them.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:16.920
I told one or two of them, Don't do it again,
because you've learnt your lesson now'.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.400
She could switch quite quickly,

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:27.000
and was clearly quite a persuasive
and highly confident person.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.760
A sociopath is probably
what you'd describe her as.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:43.680
But for whatever reasons, we can only
suspect what those reasons might be,

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:49.240
no case ever came to court and
it appears to have simply dissolved.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.120
Caparas is free,
and she got her cars back too.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:08.600
Maria Caparas first started
working in chat centres

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:13.520
where Filipino women would strip off
and talk to foreigners.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:20.360
Let's face it, it's a pretty degrading
line of work to find yourself in.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:27.280
I imagine that's perhaps where her
cynicism about the victims comes in.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:33.000
She has seen men who are behaving
in a very exploitative manner,

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:37.440
and presumably working with other people
who have been similarly exploited.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.960
It's like a telemarketing office
or a call centre,

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.040
but they are selling porn and porn sites.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:52.360
And once they saw an opportunity
of someone asking for more

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.240
At some stage, we don't know when,
but a light bulb went on,

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:00.640
and she realised how she could
turn this to her advantage.

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:03.920
It's an evil scam, but it's a very clever
scam at the same time.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.600
It plays on the fact that people are so ready

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.240
to strike up conversations
with complete strangers.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.200
They will use a persona
of a pretty young woman.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.600
The persona used would be
a younger female,

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:29.680
fun-loving, a bit silly, a bit more
of a fun and games approach.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:34.880
In social media platforms,
most of the information is available.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:42.360
They can easily go to your profile
and go through the information;

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.400
go through your hobbies, your habits,

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:50.760
go through the messages, images,
videos and all the comments,

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.120
and know who are your friends.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:58.520
The main goal for them is to make
the account as real as possible.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:05.360
Why? Because they want
the victim to trust them easily.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:21.280
20 years ago, you would never
publish your private image,

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:25.640
or hang it outside your door
so everybody could easily see it.

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:29.720
Because at that time, it was something
that was private information.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:34.480
We are freely posting
information about ourselves

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:38.680
and just giving it away
to the public and the scammers.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.800
We are just inviting them, and saying,

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:45.160
This is my life. You want to know
anything about my life, here it is.

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:47.280
And you can just have any information
about me on social media.

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:57.720
I believe today, there is a popular trend
where popularity is above privacy.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:02.720
So, the more popular you are,
the better it is.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:10.640
But again, as a choice with popularity
and having a public profile,

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:15.160
comes everything that relates
to that and the risks associated.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:19.000
That's where social platforms
are, in general,

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:23.680
a great platform for criminals
to perform their crimes.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:33.120
It's an easy way and they can hide
behind different fake identities.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.800
Basically, they use social media a lot.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:43.800
They would trawl social media websites
and interact with people,

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:47.040
and they are fishing for potential preys.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:34.920
The way sextortion works is that somebody
will send you a friend request on Facebook,

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.240
somebody you've never met before.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:57.840
If you respond to that chat, then
you can easily be hooked to the chat.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:08.200
A typical legitimate account has
around 200 to 400 Facebook friends.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.080
Statistically, when we are trying to analyse
the Facebook accounts of criminals,

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.840
you would see just around 10 friends.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:18.680
And they're foreign friends
from everywhere.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:42.800
It's a scripted narrative they use
that almost always works.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.800
And they have a mastery over the script;

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:56.080
the words to use,
the emotions to show,

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:59.840
the little attentive messages
that you can send every day

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.560
that makes somebody feel good.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:06.160
It is in this climate of trust that
they take advantage of the victim.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:24.720
We always assume,
like in those Hollywood movies,

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:29.640
somebody extremely skilful who
is running some script and codes.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:36.040
However, that is just 15% of
what's happening in cybercrimes.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:41.760
The other 85% of the cybercrime
has nothing to do with technical things,

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:46.400
it's what we call social engineering.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:51.920
Social engineering is based
on manipulating people,

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:56.760
it is very effective when you create
a certain connection with your victim

00:20:56.760 --> 00:21:01.960
and try to use that
in order to achieve your crime.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:26.600
These were mostly teenage boys, some
of whom were transitioning to be women.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:44.960
That's the age bracket of the people
who were normally arrested for sextortion

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:48.880
because they know a lot about computers.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:59.000
You can just pay these jobless teenagers
300 to 500 pesos (US$5.70 to $9.60) a day

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:03.000
and it will be enough for them.

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:11.840
You can easily lure and attract them
to these kinds of sex activities.

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:16.520
Good chatters would get
bonuses and extra rewards.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.960
She would shower them with gifts
like iPhones and Samsung phones.

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:26.800
All the arrested individuals were minors.

00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:58.680
The surroundings
is much safer for them,

00:22:58.680 --> 00:23:06.160
because there are inadequate police
authorities who operate in the area.

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:10.520
North Hills still looks like
a very ordinary village.

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:12.240
But somebody pointed out to me,

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:14.000
Have you noticed what's
different about this village?

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.920
I said, I can't. It looks like
another Filipino village to me.

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:20.200
They said, Look at the kids,
they're all wearing designer t-shirts.

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:22.920
You don't get that in a normal
Philippine village.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:29.560
She owned a large property
in the centre of the village,

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:34.520
it was like an entertainment centre for the
mostly young people who would work for her.

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.400
When we were there, there was always
crowds of kids gathering around,

00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:43.520
who were, of course, of a demographic
that would be working for her,

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:47.800
or being primed to work for her
as soon as they were a little older.

00:25:30.600 --> 00:25:33.840
If you ask anybody about Maria Caparas,

00:25:33.840 --> 00:25:39.800
they suddenly suffer from amnesia
and are reluctant to talk about it.

00:25:39.800 --> 00:25:45.680
A shopkeeper who lives near her house says
everybody knows about what's going on

00:25:45.680 --> 00:25:47.800
but nobody will talk to you about it.

00:25:47.800 --> 00:25:51.160
People are terrified to talk
about what's going on,

00:25:51.160 --> 00:25:53.840
not only terrified,
but probably invested as well.

00:25:53.840 --> 00:25:58.320
Because everybody has a son,
daughter, brother or sister

00:25:58.320 --> 00:26:02.360
somehow involved on one side
of the scam or the other.

00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:39.480
With money, you can literally buy people,

00:26:39.480 --> 00:26:44.200
and that's technically what she was doing.

00:26:46.120 --> 00:26:48.600
Maria Caparas came from
an extremely poor background,

00:26:48.600 --> 00:26:50.640
she was living in the slums in Manila.

00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:54.040
When she first arrived in the village,
the neighbours told me she was so poor

00:26:54.040 --> 00:26:57.440
that she had to beg for a bowl of rice
to feed her and her two children,

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:59.120
she had nothing at all.

00:26:59.920 --> 00:27:02.240
She's a Slumdog Millionairess effectively.

00:27:02.280 --> 00:27:06.920
She has come from nothing and become
extremely rich in an extremely dark way.

00:27:22.480 --> 00:27:26.280
&lt;i&gt;I received a random&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;Facebook request one night,&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:28.560
&lt;i&gt;from what looked like&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;an attractive female.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:33.800 --> 00:27:37.160
&lt;i&gt;At first I was resistant because&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;I didn't know this person at all.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:39.400 --> 00:27:42.800
&lt;i&gt;At the time, I didn't think nothing of it,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;like I said, so we started chatting.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:46.400 --> 00:27:49.280
&lt;i&gt;The second that we got onto the webcam,&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:49.280 --> 00:27:51.960
&lt;i&gt;this person was already&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;removing their clothing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:58.840
&lt;i&gt;I did not anticipate this, it wasn't&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;that kind of conversation prior to that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:01.000
&lt;i&gt;I just thought they wanted to talk.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:04.480 --> 00:28:05.960
&lt;i&gt;They started removing their clothing,&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:05.960 --> 00:28:10.760
&lt;i&gt;started doing some bolder things&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;with toys and stuff like that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:13.160 --> 00:28:16.240
&lt;i&gt;And then started asking me&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to remove my clothing.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:23.360
&lt;i&gt;I was resistant for a long time,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;for maybe about 15 minutes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:26.640
&lt;i&gt;I didn't really know this person,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;I didn't want to do that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:26.640 --> 00:28:29.320
&lt;i&gt;I'm not really into that whole thing either.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:29.320 --> 00:28:33.440
&lt;i&gt;But eventually, I did.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:39.760
&lt;i&gt;I showed them my private area.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:43.280 --> 00:28:46.640
&lt;i&gt;This person proceeded&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;to stop the video chat.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:51.080
&lt;i&gt;And the screen went completely blank.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:56.440
&lt;i&gt;Once that happened, I kind of&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;realised something wasn't right.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:44.280 --> 00:29:48.760
I saw Maria Caparas in prison and she
explained to me actually how it all works.

00:29:51.800 --> 00:29:55.400
She says that within 20 minutes,
the chat gets so intimate.

00:30:39.160 --> 00:30:44.680
They are pre-recorded videos
controlled by key points.

00:31:19.840 --> 00:31:21.400
There is a combination of keys

00:31:21.400 --> 00:31:27.800
to have that pre-recorded video play
as if you are really doing it for him.

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:19.640
They don't need to be IT experts or hackers.

00:32:23.080 --> 00:32:26.600
Because all this private information
has already been shared

00:32:26.600 --> 00:32:28.880
on the social media platforms.

00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:32.520
For example, if you have
working experience somewhere,

00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:36.280
you have already entered which
locations and company you work for.

00:32:36.280 --> 00:32:38.520
They don't only want you as a target,

00:32:38.520 --> 00:32:44.200
because all those friends and members
who are on your social media

00:32:44.200 --> 00:32:45.920
can be a valuable target to them.

00:33:28.080 --> 00:33:31.520
If you can record something
and play it over again,

00:33:31.520 --> 00:33:36.000
you are traumatised
each time you see it.

00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:31.240
When you are threatened that
these things will be publicly released,

00:34:31.240 --> 00:34:35.800
you literally panic,
and you get very upset.

00:34:36.480 --> 00:34:40.360
Many of these young people become
very anxious and very depressed.

00:37:01.680 --> 00:37:06.560
Whilst you have the teams of young
people running the sextortion racket,

00:37:06.560 --> 00:37:10.520
she had another team of people
helping her produce fake ID cards

00:37:10.520 --> 00:37:14.720
with which she or her lieutenants
would use to collect the money

00:37:14.720 --> 00:37:17.280
from the Western Union branches.

00:37:28.400 --> 00:37:30.800
The way it works is that
to collect these transfers,

00:37:30.800 --> 00:37:37.280
you just need an ID card that matches
the name on the transfer from overseas.

00:37:37.280 --> 00:37:40.080
And in parallel to
her sextortion business,

00:37:40.080 --> 00:37:46.560
it appears that Maria Caparas had
a cottage industry producing fake ID cards.

00:37:58.600 --> 00:38:05.880
From a money shop
that is part of the syndicate,

00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:10.560
it's much easier than withdrawing
the money from a money shop

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:13.680
that is not owned by
or part of the syndicate.

00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:20.680
So the syndicate can manipulate
the transaction and the release of money,

00:38:20.680 --> 00:38:26.720
but when you trace the money,
the details about the ID is all fictitious.

00:38:26.720 --> 00:38:28.800
-It's a fake ID.
-It's a fake ID, definitely.

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:40.320
So, for the last decade or so,

00:38:40.320 --> 00:38:43.400
we've been focusing on making
the world more open and connected.

00:38:43.400 --> 00:38:45.640
And we're not done with this yet,
we're always going to do this.

00:38:46.320 --> 00:38:50.520
But I used to think that if
we just gave people a voice,

00:38:50.520 --> 00:38:52.840
and helped some people connect,

00:38:52.840 --> 00:38:55.640
that would make the world
a lot better all by itself.

00:38:56.280 --> 00:38:58.480
And in a lot of ways, it has.

00:39:35.360 --> 00:39:38.040
It's probably the tip of the iceberg.

00:39:38.040 --> 00:39:44.200
We find that about 50% to 60% of scammers
do most of their scamming on Facebook.

00:39:53.040 --> 00:39:54.960
Facebook is the perfect platform
for the scammers

00:39:54.960 --> 00:39:58.360
because everything they need
is in that one place.

00:39:58.360 --> 00:40:02.160
They are able to meet with people
and video chat with them there.

00:40:02.160 --> 00:40:05.000
They have their lives there,
and their photographs,

00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:06.800
and a list of their friends and family,

00:40:06.800 --> 00:40:09.760
so it's just all encapsulated
in that one place for them.

00:40:16.360 --> 00:40:19.280
I'd say we get around 500 reports a month,

00:40:19.280 --> 00:40:21.360
which is about 15 a day.

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:31.600
When we originally started doing this,
around 40% of the people who come to us

00:40:31.600 --> 00:40:34.000
say that their scammer
was from the Philippines.

00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:38.440
Today, around 55% to 60% of them
would come from the Philippines.

00:40:38.440 --> 00:40:45.400
The first requirement for a person to
get involved in sextortion is the internet.

00:40:50.240 --> 00:40:54.960
It can be anywhere in the Philippines,
there is no specific location.

00:40:54.960 --> 00:40:57.120
They just need very basic things.

00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:00.280
Definitely, they need some device.

00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:19.840
This syndicate can be anywhere.

00:41:19.840 --> 00:41:25.160
They don't need to be in a certain location
to find a victim in that particular location.

00:41:25.160 --> 00:41:29.280
They can sit anywhere and
the victim can be far, far away.

00:41:29.280 --> 00:41:35.560
There is a continual increase of the
numbers of recorded sextortion cases.

00:41:40.600 --> 00:41:43.440
You can see from the statistics that...

00:41:43.440 --> 00:41:47.480
there is an increase of 100% per year.

00:41:57.680 --> 00:42:02.520
80% of our recorded sextortion
cases uses social media.

00:42:02.520 --> 00:42:06.440
There's a huge difference in
investigating a traditional crime,

00:42:06.440 --> 00:42:13.840
like a simple robbery, a case
of homicide, or a case of murder.

00:42:13.880 --> 00:42:20.040
There is a huge gap, on the
procedure of investigating cybercrimes.

00:42:20.040 --> 00:42:24.840
The people do not know or understand that
we cannot just hack into someone's system

00:42:24.920 --> 00:42:29.760
and determine who is the person
victimising them.

00:42:30.120 --> 00:42:35.280
Another thing is that the social media
administrators are outside the Philippines,

00:42:35.280 --> 00:42:36.440
they're not here.

00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:39.560
Not days or weeks,
but it took several months

00:42:39.560 --> 00:42:42.120
for us to acquire the information
that we sought.

00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:46.240
We need a lot of information
to be able to identify

00:42:46.240 --> 00:42:48.720
who are the people
behind this cybercrime.

00:42:49.720 --> 00:42:53.320
How do we know who
we are talking to in reality?

00:42:56.600 --> 00:42:59.720
We are not able to verify that identity

00:42:59.720 --> 00:43:04.080
in a way like we possibly could
in the physical world.

00:43:04.080 --> 00:43:06.120
There is no need for verification

00:43:06.120 --> 00:43:10.680
due to the fact that social media's
priority is user adoption.

00:43:10.680 --> 00:43:13.160
They want more users on their platform.

00:43:13.160 --> 00:43:18.520
We do not have a worldwide legislation
that can cover those cybercrimes,

00:43:18.520 --> 00:43:20.000
and the criminals know that.

00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:22.680
In some countries,
they do not even need to hide

00:43:22.680 --> 00:43:26.880
because they know that no one
will come and search for them.

00:44:57.200 --> 00:45:04.640
Maria Caparas was quite brazen
about the way she operated.

00:45:05.280 --> 00:45:09.240
She also posted pictures
of her 13-year-old son,

00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:12.520
lying down covered in thousand-peso notes

00:45:12.520 --> 00:45:16.480
and lots of other quite overt pictures.

00:45:18.360 --> 00:45:21.720
She was very open about
the money they were making.

00:45:22.840 --> 00:45:26.760
Celebrating Christmas and
wearing t-shirts with her name on it,

00:45:26.760 --> 00:45:31.520
calling them the All Stars North Hills
Village with a logo printed on the back,

00:45:31.520 --> 00:45:35.120
showing a thumb with a cross, the sign
you get if you're blocked on Facebook,

00:45:35.120 --> 00:45:36.520
and the words We hate this.

00:45:38.280 --> 00:45:41.240
I don't think that she personally
sees any reason to stop,

00:45:41.240 --> 00:45:43.000
so long as she can continue
getting away with it.

00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:46.760
All the signs are that she's going to
carry on getting away with it.

00:45:46.840 --> 00:45:51.880
She's the queen of sextortion
and North Hills Village is her fiefdom,

00:45:51.880 --> 00:45:54.240
her kingdom, if you'd like.

00:48:27.600 --> 00:48:30.840
There's a huge boom in social media
where wildlife trade is concerned.

00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:38.000
We started seeing an increase
in the number of people

00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:41.440
that were actively participating
on social media forums.

00:48:47.920 --> 00:48:50.320
They were interested in
buying and selling animals,

00:48:50.320 --> 00:48:52.840
they were interested
in asking about animals,

00:48:52.840 --> 00:48:54.800
they wanted to know prices.

00:48:55.640 --> 00:48:58.640
We realised that it was
really becoming quite popular.

00:49:01.720 --> 00:49:04.880
We identified 14 Facebook groups.

00:49:05.960 --> 00:49:09.040
We spent just 30 minutes a day

00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:14.200
to figure out what level of activity was
taking place in these 14 Facebook groups.

00:49:26.160 --> 00:49:30.360
More than 300 animals
were being offered for sale.

00:49:31.680 --> 00:49:33.720
We can say that they were
being offered for sale

00:49:33.720 --> 00:49:35.640
because prices were mentioned.

00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:40.320
Prices were specifically
mentioned in at least 30 posts.

00:49:43.320 --> 00:49:45.800
For just these 30 animals,

00:49:45.800 --> 00:49:51.000
the cumulative value was
about RM184,000 at that time.

00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:55.840
I think this really boils down
to an issue of demand and supply.

00:49:55.840 --> 00:49:59.960
As long as there is a demand,
the supply will consistently be there.

00:50:24.600 --> 00:50:26.880
The Wildlife Department
has got its hands full.

00:50:30.800 --> 00:50:36.440
We have been doing the best we can
in trying to curb this illegal trade.

00:51:11.680 --> 00:51:17.160
But now, the illegal traders
have become very savvy.

00:51:17.160 --> 00:51:19.880
They have gone into cyberspace,

00:51:19.880 --> 00:51:23.960
and they are selling their products
in cyberspace.

00:51:23.960 --> 00:51:29.400
Of course, with the advent of Facebook
and advertising on the internet,

00:51:29.400 --> 00:51:32.240
they are able to spread the information.

00:51:32.240 --> 00:51:34.560
And as always, when there are buyers,

00:51:34.560 --> 00:51:40.160
there will be people who will break the law
in order to try and gain a profit

00:51:40.160 --> 00:51:45.480
by selling animal parts and species
that are quite precious to us.

00:51:54.120 --> 00:51:57.320
It's really quite sad, because
you hear a baby crying.

00:51:59.760 --> 00:52:02.920
Somebody is obviously
videoing this whole experience.

00:52:02.920 --> 00:52:04.440
The box arrives,

00:52:04.440 --> 00:52:06.040
the box is opened,

00:52:06.040 --> 00:52:09.160
and a little baby in the box is just wailing.

00:52:09.160 --> 00:52:10.600
All you hear is a wail.

00:52:12.880 --> 00:52:17.480
It's about a baby animal
that is stolen from the wild.

00:52:17.480 --> 00:52:20.880
It doesn't belong in a box,
it doesn't belong in a small box.

00:52:20.880 --> 00:52:25.520
It would have been shipped by post,
and it had no right to be in that position.

00:52:50.240 --> 00:52:54.240
When you look at history, it was
the rich and famous or the royalty

00:52:54.240 --> 00:52:56.960
that used to showcase their animals.

00:53:01.080 --> 00:53:06.440
It was always linked with prestige,
status, and being somebody.

00:53:09.000 --> 00:53:12.320
If I can show that I own this animal,

00:53:12.320 --> 00:53:15.440
then I now become a person
of prestige, status,

00:53:15.440 --> 00:53:17.440
and acquisition.

00:53:17.440 --> 00:53:20.160
It is part of my wealth and
part of my trophy right now.

00:53:21.040 --> 00:53:25.400
The royalties, the kings and queens,
would then feature these animals

00:53:25.400 --> 00:53:27.920
because everybody
was curious to see them.

00:53:28.640 --> 00:53:33.280
It's probably one of the early
precursors of zoos.

00:53:33.280 --> 00:53:38.480
They used to feature these animals,
and people would come to observe them.

00:53:38.480 --> 00:53:42.840
There was a process where they would
show these animals to their friends

00:53:42.840 --> 00:53:44.200
and they would publicise it.

00:53:45.880 --> 00:53:50.680
In the social media world,
it means I'm going to get more likes.

00:53:50.680 --> 00:53:54.000
Especially if you have
a cute, fuzzy little animal

00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:57.080
that everybody is very excited about.

00:53:57.080 --> 00:54:02.320
You're going to get a lot of friends
coming to your page and liking it,

00:54:02.320 --> 00:54:03.480
and it goes viral.

00:54:03.480 --> 00:54:07.720
This is one of the ways that people
are making themselves more famous

00:54:07.720 --> 00:54:10.800
by linking themselves up
with exotic animals.

00:54:11.680 --> 00:54:15.280
To the buyer, that is somehow appealing.

00:54:15.280 --> 00:54:20.080
It gets posted online, and
gets a lot of likes and comments.

00:54:20.080 --> 00:54:23.240
Of course, there are a lot of angry people
who say that this is not right.

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:27.040
But clearly, that's not
what matters to the buyer.

00:58:31.400 --> 00:58:36.600
Social media and online platforms
have obviously made it really easy.

00:58:40.400 --> 00:58:44.640
Because now, by using this technology,

00:58:44.640 --> 00:58:48.000
they can easily target the mass market.

00:58:48.560 --> 00:58:51.080
They can publish a product,

00:58:51.080 --> 00:58:55.880
and everybody can know it
in a split second.

01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:11.400
All these platforms
do have terms and conditions.

01:03:15.400 --> 01:03:20.600
It says in the terms and conditions that
you cannot have any illegal activities.

01:03:20.600 --> 01:03:23.880
This is very clear to the public.

01:03:23.880 --> 01:03:29.040
However, obviously,
these people misuse the platform.

01:03:31.000 --> 01:03:33.600
At in the same time,
you can communicate with them.

01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:39.840
All these platforms provide a facility
to have a secure and private chat.

01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:46.480
That makes it more difficult for
investigators to access these chats

01:03:46.480 --> 01:03:51.760
and to identify the right person
behind the animal trafficking.

01:03:51.760 --> 01:03:56.640
For instance, by using encryption,
you can easily engage in a private chat.

01:03:59.040 --> 01:04:01.960
As you know, it's impossible
to break the encryption.

01:04:04.360 --> 01:04:08.680
The biggest challenge is data privacy,

01:04:08.680 --> 01:04:15.160
and how the platforms make
the data or communication private.

01:04:26.600 --> 01:04:31.360
Everybody is operating under the cover
of being behind their computers or phones,

01:04:31.360 --> 01:04:34.880
it's not always easy to identify
where these individuals are.

01:06:57.480 --> 01:06:58.760
Is this illegal?

01:07:10.160 --> 01:07:11.960
Which are legal and illegal?

01:07:43.680 --> 01:07:47.160
How do you know that these animals
are brought in illegally?

01:10:14.960 --> 01:10:18.520
For some of the illegal trade,
they are really pretty expensive.

01:10:21.760 --> 01:10:25.280
The value is equivalent to the downpayment
for a small house in Malaysia.

01:10:26.000 --> 01:10:28.520
We're not talking about RM10 or RM20,

01:10:28.520 --> 01:10:30.960
we're really talking about hundreds
and thousands of ringgit.

01:10:43.960 --> 01:10:45.480
The Malayan Tiger is very specific,

01:10:45.480 --> 01:10:48.040
in a sense that it's only found
in Peninsular Malaya.

01:10:51.040 --> 01:10:54.160
We are putting in a large effort
to conserve the tigers in Malaya,

01:10:54.160 --> 01:10:56.320
we only have less than 200 of them.

01:10:56.320 --> 01:10:59.520
But as you know, tiger parts trading
is now a worldwide market.

01:11:00.640 --> 01:11:06.440
People come here just to look for tigers,
to set up snares and catch them,

01:11:06.440 --> 01:11:12.880
because a tiger can be sold for
between US$150,000 and US$200,000.

01:11:12.880 --> 01:11:18.520
Every part of the tiger is sold
to make a profit.

01:11:18.520 --> 01:11:23.400
In our jungles, there are people
from Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos,

01:11:23.400 --> 01:11:26.760
including locals, who are hunting them.

01:11:37.960 --> 01:11:45.880
The batch of ivories confiscated consists of
3,692kg of whole and partial tusks,

01:11:45.880 --> 01:11:49.720
and 228kg of semi-finished products.

01:11:50.080 --> 01:11:51.880
These tusks are heavy.

01:11:52.880 --> 01:11:55.520
Of course, these are beads
made out of the tusks,

01:11:55.520 --> 01:11:57.120
they are not that heavy,

01:11:57.120 --> 01:12:00.160
but these tusks are heavy.

01:12:03.320 --> 01:12:04.640
This is machine-cut.

01:14:26.920 --> 01:14:32.360
We are going to show you how smugglers
commonly smuggle things on their persons.

01:14:33.840 --> 01:14:38.080
This is the most common
when they are travelling by air.

01:14:38.080 --> 01:14:40.400
For example, this is an egg vest.

01:14:40.400 --> 01:14:44.520
People have been caught trying
to smuggle eggs on themselves,

01:14:44.520 --> 01:14:48.360
sometimes it is on their body,
sometimes it's strapped on their legs.

01:14:48.360 --> 01:14:52.760
It keeps them nice and warm,
and doesn't set off any metal detectors,

01:14:52.760 --> 01:14:54.640
so the process goes through
quite smoothly.

01:14:55.160 --> 01:15:00.600
Sometimes there are also these
specially modified vests or jackets.

01:15:00.600 --> 01:15:04.000
In here, this is a fake ivory, of course.

01:15:04.960 --> 01:15:06.560
There are additional pockets.

01:15:07.240 --> 01:15:11.320
You can carry almost anything
as long as it's not metal.

01:15:11.320 --> 01:15:13.280
It won't set off the metal detectors.

01:15:14.160 --> 01:15:16.360
If you add more layers of clothing,
you get a little puffy

01:15:16.360 --> 01:15:18.520
and you won't set off any alarms.

01:15:21.320 --> 01:15:26.040
This is an example of how
tortoises are frequently smuggled,

01:15:26.040 --> 01:15:29.320
they are taped to prevent
them from moving.

01:15:30.720 --> 01:15:34.800
Every single one of them are alive
because they are for the pet trade.

01:15:36.920 --> 01:15:39.440
Another example are birds in bottles.

01:15:39.440 --> 01:15:40.880
If you go online and Google it,

01:15:40.880 --> 01:15:45.080
you'll find many pictures of birds
being smuggled like this.

01:15:45.080 --> 01:15:46.680
It has holes to let them breathe,

01:15:46.680 --> 01:15:49.920
but it is one of easiest and
fastest way to smuggle birds.

01:15:56.240 --> 01:15:57.680
Who doesn't like a book?

01:15:59.720 --> 01:16:03.520
But inside, there is a gecko.

01:16:04.680 --> 01:16:09.360
These are actual examples of how
smugglers have been arrested.

01:16:09.520 --> 01:16:11.960
We are seeing a lot of our native animals

01:16:11.960 --> 01:16:15.720
being exported for sale
somewhere else in the world.

01:16:15.720 --> 01:16:19.200
We're also seeing non-native animals
coming into the country,

01:16:19.200 --> 01:16:23.440
so there are these dynamics
as a source and as a consumer,

01:16:23.440 --> 01:16:28.200
as well as a transit country for things
that aren't really targeted to local demand.

01:16:28.200 --> 01:16:30.800
We're not saying that
this is a problem in Malaysia,

01:16:30.800 --> 01:16:32.640
this is a global problem.

01:18:05.840 --> 01:18:07.640
We have found baby gibbons

01:18:08.400 --> 01:18:10.520
We found baby sun bears

01:18:10.520 --> 01:18:12.200
It's really quite shocking.

01:18:12.200 --> 01:18:15.920
They were animals that were
considered to be totally protected

01:18:15.920 --> 01:18:18.720
under the Wildlife Conservation Act
of Peninsular Malaysia.

01:18:18.720 --> 01:18:20.160
A number of these individuals

01:18:20.160 --> 01:18:24.920
are actually offering animals
that you are not allowed to sell.

01:18:27.920 --> 01:18:31.920
The more worrying question is, how did
these individuals get these animals?

01:18:31.920 --> 01:18:34.040
The vast majority of them
were native animals,

01:18:34.040 --> 01:18:38.520
which means that people were going
into the forest and trapping them.

01:18:38.520 --> 01:18:41.160
What's really surprising and
even more shocking about this

01:18:41.160 --> 01:18:44.960
was that almost all of them
were juvenile animals.

01:18:46.360 --> 01:18:50.040
Particularly for mammals,
it is a really serious problem.

01:18:50.040 --> 01:18:54.200
When you take a baby away
from its mother and its family,

01:18:54.200 --> 01:18:56.080
you don't know
how long they will survive.

01:18:56.080 --> 01:18:59.920
Their own support system in the wild
has essentially been taken away.

01:21:04.040 --> 01:21:07.680
They had no respect for
protecting species in the wild,

01:21:07.680 --> 01:21:11.160
they had no respect for law
enforcement and the authorities.

01:21:11.160 --> 01:21:14.680
It was a crime, clear and simple,

01:21:14.680 --> 01:21:17.400
because they knew for a fact
that they were offering animals

01:21:17.400 --> 01:21:20.080
that they were not supposed
to offer for sale.

01:25:54.920 --> 01:25:56.760
World Wildlife Day.

01:25:56.920 --> 01:25:59.880
I'm declaring war against the poachers.

01:25:59.880 --> 01:26:03.280
The time has come to stop
the killing of the Malayan tigers

01:26:03.280 --> 01:26:06.840
and other wildlife
by the ruthless poachers.

01:26:07.320 --> 01:26:10.160
We have continuous programmes,

01:26:10.360 --> 01:26:13.320
whereby a special committee
has been set up

01:26:13.320 --> 01:26:17.880
and whatever information
that we have managed to pick up.

01:26:19.920 --> 01:26:26.200
Our Cyber Crime Unit knows how goods are
being transferred from one area to another,

01:26:26.600 --> 01:26:29.160
that is when we call them in.

01:27:06.280 --> 01:27:10.280
We also have help
from international agencies

01:27:10.280 --> 01:27:13.200
who have experience in this
and are advising us.

01:28:06.760 --> 01:28:08.960
That will deter them from coming in

01:28:08.960 --> 01:28:13.400
and trying to poach
our animals from the forest.

01:28:47.680 --> 01:28:53.840
We need to change these laws to make them
in line with what is happening today,

01:28:53.840 --> 01:28:57.960
and to make sure
that there is a deterrent.

01:28:57.960 --> 01:29:00.560
For those who break the law,

01:29:00.560 --> 01:29:06.160
the punishment is equally severe
and that they won't attempt to do it.

01:29:07.080 --> 01:29:12.840
These laws are in place,
and I think by 2020,

01:29:12.840 --> 01:29:15.360
we would see a lot of
amendments taking place,

01:29:15.360 --> 01:29:17.160
as far as the ministry is concerned.

01:29:18.320 --> 01:29:22.080
My message to them is:
"We are coming, be prepared."

01:29:22.080 --> 01:29:25.080
We have given orders on what to do.

01:29:25.120 --> 01:29:26.240
If you're caught,

01:29:26.240 --> 01:29:30.000
you will pay heavily
for the crime that you have committed.

